grows with dataset size\n","- High memory usage for large embeddings\n","\n","**When to use it**\n","\n","Use `IndexFlatL2` when:\n","\n","- Dataset is relatively small.\n","- Exact retrieval is important.\n","- You are prototyping a RAG application.\n","- You need a baseline to compare approximate indexes against.\n","\n","### Exact Inner Product Search: `IndexFlatIP`\n","\n","`IndexFlatIP` performs exhaustive search using inner product. This index returns the vectors with the highest inner-product scores.\n","\n","Use it when:\n","\n","- Your embedding model is trained for dot-product similarity.\n","- You want cosine similarity after normalizing vectors.\n","- You need exact search based on inner product.\n","\n","### Inverted File Index: `IndexIVFFlat`\n","\n","Approximate nearest-neighbor search. IVF stands for Inverted File Index. It is one of the most important FAISS indexes for large-scale retrieval.\n","\n","**The problem with Flat Search**\n","\n","Suppose you have 10 million document embeddings. Flat search compares your query against all 10 million vectors. Instead, what if we divided the vectors into clusters? That is the core idea of IVF.\n","\n","![IVF](ivf.png)\n","\n","**How IVF works**\n","\n","Imagine 10 million vectors are divided into 1,000 clusters. Each cluster has a centroid. The centroids are generated using K-means clustering.\n","\n","When a query comes in:\n","\n","1. Convert the query into a vector.\n","2. Find the nearest cluster centroids.\n","3. Select a few clusters.\n","4. Search only the vectors inside those selected clusters.\n","5. Return the top-k results.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","| Cluster      | Number of vectors |\n","| ------------ | ----------------- |\n","| Cluster 1    | 10,000            |\n","| Cluster 2    | 10,000            |\n","| Cluster 3    | 10,000            |\n","| ...          | ...               |\n","| Cluster 1000 | 10,000            |\n","\n","If we search only 10 clusters, we might examine around 100,000 vectors instead of 10 million.\n","\n","That can significantly reduce the search cost.\n","\n","**Important IVF parameters**\n","\n","| Parameter | Meaning                     |\n","| --------- | --------------------------- |\n","| `nlist`   | Number of clusters          |\n","| `nprobe`  | Number of clusters searched |\n","| `d`       | Embedding dimension         |\n","| `k`       | Number of results returned  |\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":78,"id":"ea103481","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.352276Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.351885Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.355975Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.355245Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.028183,"end_time":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.357653+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.32947+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["# Coarse quantizer\n","quantizer = faiss.IndexFlatL2(dimension)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":79,"id":"bd0c8e96","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.402674Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.401909Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.407172Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.406396Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.029751,"end_time":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.408726+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.378975+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["<faiss.swigfaiss.IndexFlatL2; proxy of <Swig Object of type 'faiss::IndexFlatL2 *' at 0x7bba3ab0a570> >"]},"execution_count":79,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["quantizer"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":80,"id":"6ba24efc","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.453002Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.452196Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.456547Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-13T06:32:42.455728Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.028495,